# Skill: mobile

Use this skill when testing, verifying, or automating mobile interactions on
{% if ui_mobile_ios and ui_mobile_android %}iOS and Android{% elif ui_mobile_ios %}iOS{% else %}Android{% endif %}.

## Tool to use

Use the Appium MCP connector (`appium_*` tools) — not a desktop browser automation tool.

## Session setup

```
1. select_device       → choose simulator/emulator or real device
2. appium_session_management (action=create)  → start a session
3. navigate to the feature under test
4. run the scenario steps
5. appium_session_management (action=delete)  → close session
```

## Locator hierarchy (most to least preferred)

```
accessibility id        → most stable, maps to accessibilityIdentifier (iOS) / contentDescription (Android)
id                      → resource-id (Android) / name (iOS)
xpath                   → use only when nothing else works; prefer short paths
```

## Evidence rules

- Screenshot every Given/When/Then step (use `appium_screenshot`)
- Screenshots capture the full device screen — annotate which element is the focus if
  the region is not obvious
- Save screenshots under `evidence/<TICKET-KEY>/<scenario-slug>/`

{% if ui_mobile_ios %}
## iOS-specific notes

- Test on the iOS Simulator (Xcode) before real device
- Use `prepare_ios_simulator` before the first session if the simulator is cold
- Accessibility IDs are the most reliable locator — ask devs to add them if missing
- Gestures: use `appium_gesture` (tap, swipe, scroll); `appium_perform_actions` for
  complex multi-touch

{% endif %}
{% if ui_mobile_android %}
## Android-specific notes

- Test on the Android Emulator (AVD) before real device
- `contentDescription` is the closest equivalent to iOS `accessibilityIdentifier`
- Use `appium_mobile_keyboard` for text input on Android (avoid direct `send_keys` for
  special characters)

{% endif %}

## Common gotchas

| Symptom | Likely cause |
|---|---|
| Element not found | App not fully loaded — add an explicit wait |
| Intermittent tap failure | Element partially obscured by keyboard — scroll it into view |
| Session fails to create | Simulator/emulator not booted — call `prepare_ios_simulator` or start AVD |
| Wrong screen after action | Navigation animation still in progress — wait for the target screen's marker element |
